But wait - what if `b == end - 1` and `b[0] == '\r'`? Then `b < end - 1` is false, so the first `if` is skipped. Then `b < end - 1` is false, so the second `if` is skipped. `last = b = end - 1`. Then `b++` makes `b = end`. The loop condition `b < end` fails. So `last = end - 1`. Then `ms->search.s_len = last - buf = end - 1 - buf = bytecnt - 1`. This is fine.

But what if `b == end - 1` and `b[0] == '\r'` and `b[1]` is read? No, the condition `b < end - 1` is checked first, so `b[1]` is only read when `b < end - 1`, meaning `b + 1 < end`, so `b[1]` is valid.

